{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A representation of a block of HTTP header fields."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPHeaders","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"HTTP header fields are a complex data structure. The most natural representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for these is a sequence of two-tuples of field name and field value, both as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"strings. This structure preserves that representation, but provides a number of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"convenience features in addition to it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, this structure enables access to header fields based on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"case-insensitive form of the field name, but preserves the original case of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field when needed. It also supports recomposing headers to a maximally joined","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or split representation, such that header fields that are able to be repeated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be represented appropriately.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/sotosignerv4\/httpheaders"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/codes.soto.soto-core\/SK","doc:\/\/codes.soto.soto-core\/Sl","doc:\/\/codes.soto.soto-core\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/codes.soto.soto-core\/SQ","doc:\/\/codes.soto.soto-core\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/codes.soto.soto-cor